## 2. Raw API Response → What Fields Come In

### OE API Fields (Online Orders)
| API field | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| [id](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/data_loader.py#492-511) | Order ID |
| `order_date` / `created_at` | When order was placed |
| [order_status](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/main.py#1850-1972) | `Delivered Orders`, `Cancelled Orders`, `Returned Orders`, `Pending Orders`, `Courier In-Process`, `Dealer Orders`, `Awaiting Approval`, `LHR/KHI Warehouse Orders`, `Dispatched Orders`, `Refund Orders` |
| `customer_name` | Full name |
| `customer_phone` | Phone string |
| `customer_city` | City text |
| `customer_state` | Province (OE uses `customer_state`) |
| `customer_address` | Full address |
| `customer_email` | Email |
| `total_price` | Order total |
| `payment_mode` | `Cash`, `Bank Transfer`, etc. |
| `brand_name` | Brand |
| `order_name` | Human-readable name |
| `has_items[]` | Array of line items (OE uses `has_items`) |
| **Item fields:** [id](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/data_loader.py#492-511) (product_id), `title` (name), `sku`, `product_type`, `quantity`, `price`, `base_price` |

### POS API Fields (In-Store/Dealer)
| API field | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| [id](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/data_loader.py#492-511) | Order ID |
| `customer_phone` / `phone` | Customer phone |
| `customer_name` / `name` | Name |
| `customer_city` / [city](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/main.py#2095-2191) | City (or from `dealer.city` if blank) |
| `order_date` / [date](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/data_loader.py#492-511) | Date |
| `total` / `total_price` | Total |
| `payment_mode` | Payment method |
| [order_status](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/main.py#1850-1972) / [status](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/services/scheduler.py#207-218) | Always `completed` for POS |
| `dealer.province` | Province (POS uses nested dealer object) |
| `items[]` / `order_items[]` | Line items |
| **Item fields:** [product_id](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/main.py#5994-6044), `name`, `sku`, `quantity`, `price`, `unit_price` |

> ⚠️ **Key difference:** OE items use `has_items` + `title`, POS uses [items](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/scripts/setup_database.py#124-157) + `name`. Both are handled by the [transform_order_data()](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/services/sync_service.py#169-235) function.

