## 3. Transformation Logic (`services/sync_service.py → transform_order_data()`)

```
Raw API order
    │
    ▼
1. unified_customer_id = f"{customer_phone}_{customer_name}".strip('_')
2. province:
     OE → order.customer_state
     POS → order.dealer.province  (falls back if customer field empty)
3. customer_city:
     OE → order.customer_city
     POS → order.customer_city OR order.dealer.city
4. items loop → build items_json array:
     product_id = item.id OR item.product_id OR item.sku
     product_name = item.title OR item.product_name OR item.name
     sku = item.sku (only reliable in OE)
     category = item.product_type  (only real in OE; POS sends "simple" → cleared)
     quantity = item.quantity
     price = item.price
     unit_price = item.base_price OR item.unit_price OR item.price
5. order_type = "OE" or "POS"
6. items_json stored as JSONB in orders table
   items list used to insert into order_items table
```

**Province fallback chain** (in [local_ml_pipeline.py](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/scripts/local_ml_pipeline.py)):  
`order.customer_province` → `order.province` → [get_province_from_city(city)](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/scripts/local_ml_pipeline.py#226-233) → city-to-province mapping table

