## 6. Insert Strategy (Upsert)

```sql
-- Orders: upsert on conflict
INSERT INTO orders (id, order_type, ..., items_json)
VALUES (%s, ...)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET
    updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    synced_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    province = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.province, orders.province),
    source_type = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.source_type, orders.source_type)

-- Order items: insert, skip if exists
INSERT INTO order_items (order_id, product_id, product_name, quantity, unit_price, total_price)
VALUES (...)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
```

Uses **SAVEPOINT** per order — if one order fails, the transaction continues (no full rollback).

---

## 7. Data Issues Found

> [!CAUTION]
> **`customer_phone` is NULL in sampled orders.** The `unified_customer_id` is built from `phone_name`, but if phone is empty, IDs become `_name_only` — breaking customer identity linking.

> [!WARNING]
> **Duplicate province names:** `Islamabad` ≠ `Islamabad Capital Territory` — 673 orders have the longer variant. The [normalize_province()](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/main.py#426-448) function handles this in SQL queries but NOT during insert.

> [!WARNING]
> **order_items rows (230K) < orders rows (289K):** Many orders have no items in [order_items](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/scripts/setup_database.py#124-157) table — their products are stored only in `items_json` JSONB column. The `populate_order_items_from_orders()` stored function should be run to normalize these.

> [!NOTE]
> **Dual product_id strategy:** OE uses numeric Shopify product IDs (e.g., `1297`), POS uses SKU strings. This means the same physical product can have two different [product_id](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/main.py#5994-6044) values depending on the source — important for recommendation deduplication.
